# __PROJECT__ specifications

How this spec tree is organized, and the rules that keep it usable. Read this before adding an epic
or cutting a release.

## Layout

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `overview.md` | Objective, success criteria, non-goals |
| `decisions.md` | Locked architectural decisions |
| `progress.md` | Append-only build log — what shipped, when |
| `backlog.md` | Deferred and not-yet-scoped work |
| `epics/E<n>-<slug>/` | An epic: its features, each feature its stories |
| `releases/release-<n>/` | A delivery slice: which stories ship, entry and exit criteria |

## Rules

- **IDs are permanent.** `E<n>` epic, `F<n>.<m>` feature, `S<n>.<m>.<k>` story. Reorganizing never
  renumbers; a story that moves keeps its ID and notes where it came from. Gaps are fine.
- **One home per story.** A story's text lives in its feature file. Release pages link to it by ID
  and never restate it.
- **Status lives on the story.** Epic indexes and release pages derive status by reference rather
  than carrying their own copy.
- **`progress.md` is never sharded.** Status has to stay answerable in one read.
- **A story belongs to one release at a time**, recorded on the release page, not on the story.

